  "summary": "Researchers combined case and testing records from Ituri province, DR Congo, with human mobility data to study the first weeks of a Bundibugyo virus outbreak. Between May 10 and June 1, affected health zones rose by 12 and health areas by 49, with movement as a main driver of the spread. The estimate covers only the early phase and depends on how complete early detection was.",
